e is nice to animals), he cannot be one of the grumpy people who are mean to animals. However, this does not rule out the possibility that Tom is grumpy in a way that does not involve being mean to animals.\n\nTherefore, we cannot definitively conclude whether Tom is grumpy or not based solely on the given information. Tom could be grumpy in a way that does not involve being mean to animals, or he could be neither grumpy nor mean to animals.\n\nThus, the statement "Tom is a grumpy person" is uncertain.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
