messages:   17%|#7        | 35/204 [02:21<00:19,  8.70it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James does not have a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain. I think the correct option is: B\n', '<think>\nTo determine if the statement "James does not have a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain, let\'s analyze the given information step by step:\n\n1. **No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**\n   - This means if a student works in the library, they cannot be from the computer science department.\n\n2. **All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.**\n   - This implies that if a student has a part-time job offered by the university, they must work in the library.\n\n3. **All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**\n   - This means if a student takes the database course, they must be from the computer science department.\n\n4. **All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**\n   - This means if a student is instructed by professor David, they are taking the database course.\n\n5. **All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.**\n   - This means if a student works in the lab, they are instructed by professor David.\n\n6. **James is a student working in the lab.**\n   - From point 5, since James works in the lab, he is instructed by professor David.\n\n7. **All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**\n   - Since James is instructed by professor David, he must be taking the database course.\n\n8. **All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**\n   - Since James is taking the database course, he must be from the computer science department.\n\n9. **No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**\n   - Since James is from the computer science department (from point 8), he cannot work in the library (from point 1).\n\n10. **All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.**\n    - Since James cannot work in the library (from point 9), he does not have a part-time job offered by the university.\n\nBased on the logical deductions from the given information, we can conclude that James does not have a part-time job offered by the university.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
