health-conscious childhood home.\n\n4. **If people have good relationships with their parents, then they fulfill their nutritional daily intakes.**\n   - This means if Taylor has a good relationship with her parents, she fulfills her nutritional daily intakes.\n\n5. **If people have good relationships with their parents, then they do not eat salads regularly.**\n   - This means if Taylor has a good relationship with her parents, she does not eat salads regularly.\n\n6. **If people visit the gym at least once a day, then they always fulfill their daily nutritional intakes.**\n   - This means if Taylor visits the gym at least once a day, she always fulfills her daily nutritional intakes.\n\n7. **It is either both true that Taylor grew up in a health-conscious childhood home and she has a good relationship with her parents, or it is true that Taylor neither grew up in a health-conscious childhood home nor has a good relationship with her parents.**\n   - This is a conditional statement that can be broken down into two cases:\n     - Case 1: Taylor grew up in a health-conscious childhood home and she has a good relationship with her parents.\n     - Case 2: Taylor neither grew up in a health-conscious childhood home nor has a good relationship with her parents.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze each case:\n\n**Case 1: Taylor grew up in a health-conscious childhood home and she has a good relationship with her parents.**\n- If Taylor grew up in a health-conscious childhood home, she eats salads regularly (from point 2).\n- If Taylor has a good relationship with her parents, she does not eat salads regularly (from point 5).\n- This creates a contradiction because Taylor cannot simultaneously eat salads regularly and not eat salads regularly.\n\n**Case 2: Taylor neither grew up in a health-conscious childhood home nor has a good relationship with her parents.**\n- If Taylor neither grew up in a health-conscious childhood home nor has a good relationship with her parents, she does not eat salads regularly (from point 5).\n\nSince both cases lead to contradictions, the only consistent scenario is that Taylor neither grew up in a health-conscious childhood home nor has a good relationship with her parents. Therefore, based on this analysis, Taylor does not eat salads regularly.\n\nGiven this reasoning, the statement "Taylor eats salads regularly" is false.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 38%|###7      | 77/204 [02:26<00:13,  9.25it/s] 38%|###8      | 78/204 [02:26<00:13,  9.09it/s]
