he key condition that needs to be satisfied for Tom to rent an apartment in a managed building.\n\nNow, let\'s analyze the conditions for Tom to rent an apartment in The Olive Garden:\n\n- **Managed Building**: The Olive Garden is a managed building, so this condition is satisfied.\n- **Pets Allowed**: We need to determine if pets are allowed in The Olive Garden. The context does not explicitly state whether pets are allowed, so we cannot conclude this part from the given information.\n- **Security Deposit**: The security deposit can be either $2000 or more than $2000. Since the statement says the deposit is no more than $1500, this condition is not satisfied.\n\nGiven that the security deposit condition is not met (it must be no more than $1500, but it is $2000), Tom will not rent an apartment in The Olive Garden.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Tom will rent an apartment in The Olive Garden" is false.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
