, we can conclude the following:\n- Steinhauer was the winner.\n- Steinhauer participated in the event.\n- Descampe, who is from Belgium and on the leaderboard, participated in the event.\n- Since there was a six-way tie, and Steinhauer was the winner, it means that the other five players in the tie were not the winner.\n\nTherefore, the statement "Steinhauer was not the winner of the 1992 du Maurier Classic" is false.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
